#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:391
msgid "Packages"
msgstr "Balíčky"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:393
msgid ""
"Packages are a way of structuring Python's module namespace by using "
"\"dotted module names\".  For example, the module name :mod:`!A.B` "
"designates a submodule named ``B`` in a package named ``A``.  Just like the "
"use of modules saves the authors of different modules from having to worry "
"about each other's global variable names, the use of dotted module names "
"saves the authors of multi-module packages like NumPy or Pillow from having "
"to worry about each other's module names."
msgstr ""
"Balicky jsou zpusobem, jak strukturovat modul namespace Pythonu pouzitim "
"\"teckovanych jmen modulu\". Naprklad jmeno modulu :mod:`!A.B` oznacuje "
"podmodul nazvan ``B`` v balicku nazvanem ``A``. Stejne jako pouziti modulu "
"uchovava autory ruznych modulu od khroniky v zabezpeceni o kolizni "
"globalnimi jmeny promennych, pouziti teckovanych jmen modulu uchovava autory"
" multi-modulu balicku jako NumPy nebo Pillow od starostlenosti o jmenach "
"ostatnich modulu."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:401
msgid ""
"Suppose you want to design a collection of modules (a \"package\") for the "
"uniform handling of sound files and sound data.  There are many different "
"sound file formats (usually recognized by their extension, for example: "
":file:`.wav`, :file:`.aiff`, :file:`.au`), so you may need to create and "
"maintain a growing collection of modules for the conversion between the "
"various file formats. There are also many different operations you might "
"want to perform on sound data (such as mixing, adding echo, applying an "
"equalizer function, creating an artificial stereo effect), so in addition "
"you will be writing a never-ending stream of modules to perform these "
"operations.  Here's a possible structure for your package (expressed in "
"terms of a hierarchical filesystem):"
msgstr ""
"Predpokladejme, ze chcete navrhnout kolekci modulu (\"balic\") pro jednotne "
"zpracovani zvukovych souboru a zvukovych dat. Existuje mnoho rozdilnych "
"formatu zvukovych souboru (obvykle rozpoznavane jejich rozsirenim, napr: "
":file:`.wav`, :file:`.aiff`, :file:`.au`), takze mozna budete muset vytvaret"
" a udrzovat rostouci kolekci modulu pro konverzi mezi ruznymi formaty "
"souboru. Existuji take mnohde rozdilne operace, ktere byste mohli chtit "
"provest na zvukovych datech (jako jsou miching, pridavani echo, aplikace "
"ekvalizeru, vytvareni umeleho stereo efektu), takze jeste budete psani nikdy"
" nekoncici toku modulu provest tyto operace. Zde je mozna struktura pro vas "
"balic (vyjadrena z hlediska hierarchickeho filesystemu):"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:412
msgid ""
"sound/                          Top-level package\n"
"      __init__.py               Initialize the sound package\n"
"      formats/                  Subpackage for file format conversions\n"
"              __init__.py\n"
"              wavread.py\n"
"              wavwrite.py\n"
"              aiffread.py\n"
"              aiffwrite.py\n"
"              auread.py\n"
"              auwrite.py\n"
"              ...\n"
"      effects/                  Subpackage for sound effects\n"
"              __init__.py\n"
"              echo.py\n"
"              surround.py\n"
"              reverse.py\n"
"              ...\n"
"      filters/                  Subpackage for filters\n"
"              __init__.py\n"
"              equalizer.py\n"
"              vocoder.py\n"
"              karaoke.py\n"
"              ..."
msgstr ""
"sound/                          Balicek na nejvyssi urovni\n"
"      __init__.py               Inicializace balicku sound\n"
"      formats/                  Podbalic pro konverze formatu souboru\n"
"              __init__.py\n"
"              wavread.py\n"
"              wavwrite.py\n"
"              aiffread.py\n"
"              aiffwrite.py\n"
"              auread.py\n"
"              auwrite.py\n"
"              ...\n"
"      effects/                  Podbalic pro zvukove efekty\n"
"              __init__.py\n"
"              echo.py\n"
"              surround.py\n"
"              reverse.py\n"
"              ...\n"
"      filters/                  Podbalic pro filtry\n"
"              __init__.py\n"
"              equalizer.py\n"
"              vocoder.py\n"
"              karaoke.py\n"
"              ..."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:438
msgid ""
"When importing the package, Python searches through the directories on "
"``sys.path`` looking for the package subdirectory."
msgstr ""
"Pri importovani balicku Python vyhledava adresar na ``sys.path`` ktery hleda"
" podadresarovy balic."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:441
msgid ""
"The :file:`__init__.py` files are required to make Python treat directories "
"containing the file as packages (unless using a :term:`namespace package`, a"
" relatively advanced feature). This prevents directories with a common name,"
" such as ``string``, from unintentionally hiding valid modules that occur "
"later on the module search path. In the simplest case, :file:`__init__.py` "
"can just be an empty file, but it can also execute initialization code for "
"the package or set the ``__all__`` variable, described later."
msgstr ""
"Soubory :file:`__init__.py` jsou povinne, aby Python zachazal s adresy "
"obsahujicimi soubor jako balicky (pokud se nepouziva :term:`namespace "
"package`, pomerne pokrocila funkce). Toto brani adresarium se spolecnym "
"jmenem, jako ``string``, aby nechtene neskryvala platne moduly, ktere se "
"objevuji pozdeji na ceste hledani modulu. V jednoduchsim pripade muze byt "
":file:`__init__.py` jen prazdny soubor, ale muze take provest inicializacni "
"kod pro balic nebo nastavit promennou ``__all__``, popsanou pozdeji."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:449
msgid ""
"Users of the package can import individual modules from the package, for "
"example::"
msgstr "Uzivate balicku mohou importovat jednotlive moduly z balicku, napr::"

