msgstr "echo.echofilter(input, output, delay=0.7, atten=4)"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:468
msgid ""
"Yet another variation is to import the desired function or variable "
"directly::"
msgstr ""
"Jeste jiny variace je importovat pozadovanou funkci nebo promennou primo::"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:470
msgid "from sound.effects.echo import echofilter"
msgstr "from sound.effects.echo import echofilter"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:472
msgid ""
"Again, this loads the submodule :mod:`!echo`, but this makes its function "
":func:`!echofilter` directly available::"
msgstr ""
"Opet, toto nacta podmodul :mod:`!echo`, ale toto cini jeho funkci "
":func:`!echofilter` primo dostupnou::"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:475
msgid "echofilter(input, output, delay=0.7, atten=4)"
msgstr "echofilter(input, output, delay=0.7, atten=4)"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:477
msgid ""
"Note that when using ``from package import item``, the item can be either a "
"submodule (or subpackage) of the package, or some  other name defined in the"
" package, like a function, class or variable.  The ``import`` statement "
"first tests whether the item is defined in the package; if not, it assumes "
"it is a module and attempts to load it.  If it fails to find it, an "
":exc:`ImportError` exception is raised."
msgstr ""
"Poznamejte, ze pri pouziti ``from package import item``, polozka muze byt "
"buď podmodul (nebo podbalic) balicku, nebo nektere jine jmeno definovane v "
"balicku, jako funkce, trida nebo promenna. Prikaz ``import`` se nejprve "
"testuje, zda je polozka definovana v balicku; pokud ne, predpoklada se, ze "
"jde o modul a pokusy se jej nactou. Pokud se mu nepodari jej najit, je "
"vyvozena vyjimka :exc:`ImportError`."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:484
msgid ""
"Contrarily, when using syntax like ``import item.subitem.subsubitem``, each "
"item except for the last must be a package; the last item can be a module or"
" a package but can't be a class or function or variable defined in the "
"previous item."
msgstr ""
"Naopak, pri pouziti syntaxe jako ``import item.subitem.subsubitem``, kazdá "
"polozka s vyjimkou posledni musi byt balic; posledni polozka muze byt modul "
"nebo balic, ale nemůze byt trida nebo funkce nebo promenna definovana v "
"predchozi polozce."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:493
msgid "Importing \\* From a Package"
msgstr "Import \\ * Z balicku"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:497
msgid ""
"Now what happens when the user writes ``from sound.effects import *``?  "
"Ideally, one would hope that this somehow goes out to the filesystem, finds "
"which submodules are present in the package, and imports them all.  This "
"could take a long time and importing sub-modules might have unwanted side-"
"effects that should only happen when the sub-module is explicitly imported."
msgstr ""
"Nyní, co se stane, když uživatel napíše ``from sound.effects import *``? V "
"ideálním případě bychom doufali, že se to nějak dostane do systému souborů, "
"najde, které podmoduly jsou přítomny v balíčku, a naimportuje je všechny. "
"Toto by mohlo trvat dlouho a import submodulů by mohl mít nežádoucí vedlejší"
" účinky, které by měly nastat pouze v případě, že je submodul explicitně "
"importován."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:503
msgid ""
"The only solution is for the package author to provide an explicit index of "
"the package.  The :keyword:`import` statement uses the following convention:"
" if a package's :file:`__init__.py` code defines a list named ``__all__``, "
"it is taken to be the list of module names that should be imported when "
"``from package import *`` is encountered.  It is up to the package author to"
" keep this list up-to-date when a new version of the package is released.  "
"Package authors may also decide not to support it, if they don't see a use "
"for importing \\* from their package.  For example, the file "
":file:`sound/effects/__init__.py` could contain the following code::"
msgstr ""
"Jedinou řešením je, aby autor balíčku poskytl explicitní rejstřík balíčku. "
"Příkaz :keyword:`import` používá následující konvenci: pokud kód "
":file:`__init__.py` balíčku definuje seznam s názvem ``__all__``, je "
"považován za seznam jmen modulů, které by měly být importovány, když je "
"``from package import *`` zjištěn. Je na autorovi balíčku, aby tento seznam "
"udržoval v aktuálním stavu, když je vydána nová verze balíčku. Autoři "
"balíčků se mohou také rozhodnout jej nepodporovat, pokud nevidí důvod pro "
"import \\* z jejich balíčku. Například soubor "
":file:`sound/effects/__init__.py` by mohl obsahovat následující kód::"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:513
msgid "__all__ = [\"echo\", \"surround\", \"reverse\"]"
msgstr "__all__ = [\"echo\", \"surround\", \"reverse\"]"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:515
msgid ""
"This would mean that ``from sound.effects import *`` would import the three "
"named submodules of the :mod:`!sound.effects` package."
msgstr ""
"To by znamenalo, ze ``from sound.effects import *`` by importoval tri "
"pojmenovane podmoduly balicku :mod:`!sound.effects`."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:518
msgid ""
"Be aware that submodules might become shadowed by locally defined names. For"
" example, if you added a ``reverse`` function to the "
":file:`sound/effects/__init__.py` file, the ``from sound.effects import *`` "
"would only import the two submodules ``echo`` and ``surround``, but *not* "
"the ``reverse`` submodule, because it is shadowed by the locally defined "
"``reverse`` function::"
msgstr ""
"Budte si vedomi, ze podmoduly mohou byt stineny lokalne definovanymi jmeny. "
"Naprklad, pokud jste pridali funkci ``reverse`` do souboru "
":file:`sound/effects/__init__.py`, ``from sound.effects import *`` by "
"importoval pouze dva podmoduly ``echo`` a ``surround``, ale *ne* podmodul "
"``reverse``, proto ze je stinen lokalne definovanou funkci ``reverse``::"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:525
msgid ""
"__all__ = [\n"
"    \"echo\",      # refers to the 'echo.py' file\n"
"    \"surround\",  # refers to the 'surround.py' file\n"
"    \"reverse\",   # !!! refers to the 'reverse' function now !!!\n"
"]\n"
"\n"
"def reverse(msg: str):  # <-- this name shadows the 'reverse.py' submodule\n"
"    return msg[::-1]    #     in the case of a 'from sound.effects import *'"
msgstr ""
"__all__ = [\n"
"    \"echo\",      # odkazuje na soubor 'echo.py'\n"
"    \"surround\",  # odkazuje na soubor 'surround.py'\n"
"    \"reverse\",   # !!! odkazuje na funkci 'reverse' nyn !!!\n"
"]\n"
"\n"
"def reverse(msg: str):  # <-- toto jmeno stini podmodul 'reverse.py'\n"
"    return msg[::-1]    #     v pripade 'from sound.effects import *'"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:534
msgid ""
"If ``__all__`` is not defined, the statement ``from sound.effects import *``"
" does *not* import all submodules from the package :mod:`!sound.effects` "
"into the current namespace; it only ensures that the package "
":mod:`!sound.effects` has been imported (possibly running any initialization"
" code in :file:`__init__.py`) and then imports whatever names are defined in"
" the package.  This includes any names defined (and submodules explicitly "
"loaded) by :file:`__init__.py`.  It also includes any submodules of the "
"package that were explicitly loaded by previous :keyword:`import` "
"statements.  Consider this code::"
msgstr ""
"Pokud neni ``__all__`` definovan, prikaz ``from sound.effects import *`` "
"*ne* importuje vsechny podmoduly z balicku :mod:`!sound.effects` do "
"aktualniho menneho prostoru; pouze zajisti, ze balic :mod:`!sound.effects` "
"byl importovan (mozna se spoustejici inicializacni kod v "
":file:`__init__.py`) a pak importuje jakekoli jmena definovana v balicku. To"
" obsahuje jakekoli jmena definovana (a podmoduly explicitne nactene) "
":file:`__init__.py`. Obsahuje take jakekoli podmoduly balicku, ktere byly "
"explicitne nacteny predchozimi prikazy :keyword:`import`. Zvazte tento kod::"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:543
msgid ""
"import sound.effects.echo\n"
"import sound.effects.surround\n"
"from sound.effects import *"
msgstr ""
"import sound.effects.echo\n"
"import sound.effects.surround\n"
"from sound.effects import *"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:547
msgid ""
"In this example, the :mod:`!echo` and :mod:`!surround` modules are imported "
"in the current namespace because they are defined in the "
":mod:`!sound.effects` package when the ``from...import`` statement is "
"executed.  (This also works when ``__all__`` is defined.)"
msgstr ""
"V tomto pripade jsou moduly :mod:`!echo` a :mod:`!surround` importovany v "
"aktualnim mennem prostoru, protože jsou definovany v balicku "
":mod:`!sound.effects` kdyz je prikaz ``from...import`` vykona. (To funguje i"
" kdyz je ``__all__`` definovan.)"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:552
msgid ""
"Although certain modules are designed to export only names that follow "
"certain patterns when you use ``import *``, it is still considered bad "
"practice in production code."
msgstr ""
"Pres to, ze nektere moduly jsou navrzeny k exportu pouze jmen, ktera se ridi"
" urcitymi vzory kdyz pouzijete ``import *``, je stale povazovano za spanou "
"praxi v produkci kodu."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:556
msgid ""
"Remember, there is nothing wrong with using ``from package import "
"specific_submodule``!  In fact, this is the recommended notation unless the "
"importing module needs to use submodules with the same name from different "
"packages."
msgstr ""
"Pamatujte, neni nic spatnehova na pouziti ``from package import "
"specific_submodule``! Ve skutecnosti je to dopoducena notace, pokud "
"importujici modul nepotrebuje pouzivat podmoduly se stejnym jmenem z ruznych"
" balicku."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:565
msgid "Intra-package References"
msgstr "Odkazy uvnitř balíčku"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:567
msgid ""
"When packages are structured into subpackages (as with the :mod:`!sound` "
"package in the example), you can use absolute imports to refer to submodules"
" of siblings packages.  For example, if the module "
":mod:`!sound.filters.vocoder` needs to use the :mod:`!echo` module in the "
":mod:`!sound.effects` package, it can use ``from sound.effects import "
"echo``."
msgstr ""
"Kdyz jsou balicky strukturovany do podbalicku (jako s balickem :mod:`!sound`"
" v priklad), muzete pouzivat absolutni importy k odkazovani na podmoduly "
"sestra balicku. Naprklad, pokud modul :mod:`!sound.filters.vocoder` "
"potrebuje pouzivat modul :mod:`!echo` v balicku :mod:`!sound.effects`, muze "
"pouzivat ``from sound.effects import echo``."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:573
msgid ""
"You can also write relative imports, with the ``from module import name`` "
"form of import statement.  These imports use leading dots to indicate the "
"current and parent packages involved in the relative import.  From the "
":mod:`!surround` module for example, you might use::"
msgstr ""
"Muzu take psát relativni importy, s tvar ``from module import name`` importu"
" prikazu. Tyto importy pouzivaji uvedene tecky k indikaci aktualniho a "
"rodicovskych balicku zapojenych do relativniho importu. Z modulu "
":mod:`!surround` naprklad byste mohli pouzivat::"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:578
msgid ""
"from . import echo\n"
"from .. import formats\n"
"from ..filters import equalizer"
msgstr ""
"from . import echo\n"
"from .. import formats\n"
"from ..filters import equalizer"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:582
msgid ""
"Note that relative imports are based on the name of the current module's "
"package. Since the main module does not have a package, modules intended for"
" use as the main module of a Python application must always use absolute "
"imports."
msgstr ""
"Poznamejte, ze relativni importy jsou zalozeny na jmenu aktualnich modulu "
"balicku. Vzdy ci hlavni modul nema balic, moduly urcenije pro pouziti jako "
"hlavni modul aplikace Pythonu musi vzdy pouzivat absolutni importy."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:588
msgid "Packages in Multiple Directories"
msgstr "Balíčky ve více adresářích"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:590
msgid ""
"Packages support one more special attribute, :attr:`~module.__path__`.  This"
" is initialized to be a :term:`sequence` of strings containing the name of "
"the directory holding the package's :file:`__init__.py` before the code in "
"that file is executed.  This variable can be modified; doing so affects "
"future searches for modules and subpackages contained in the package."
msgstr ""
"Balíčky podporují jeden další speciální atribut, :attr:`~module.__path__`. "
"Ten je inicializován jako :term:`sekvence <sequence>` řetězců obsahující "
"jméno adresáře obsahujícího :file:`__init__.py` balíčku před spuštěním kódu "
"v tomto souboru. Tato proměnná může být upravena; její změna ovlivňuje "
"budoucí hledání modulů a podbalíčků obsažených v balíčku."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:597
msgid ""
"While this feature is not often needed, it can be used to extend the set of "
"modules found in a package."
msgstr ""
"Zatimco tato funkce neni casto potreba, muze se pouzivat k rozsireni sady "
"modulu nalezene v balicku."

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:602
msgid "Footnotes"
msgstr "Poznámky pod čarou"

#: ../../tutorial/modules.rst:603
msgid ""
"In fact function definitions are also 'statements' that are 'executed'; the "
"execution of a module-level function definition adds the function name to "
"the module's global namespace."
msgstr ""
"Ve skutecnosti jsou definice funkci take 'prikazy', ktere jsou 'vykonany'; "
"vykonani definice funkce na urovni modulu prida jmeno funkce do globalniho "
"menneho prostoru modulu."

